<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Data extraction rules (Android 12+ / API 31+).

   See https://developer.android.com/about/versions/12/backup-restore#xml-changes

   The `<exclude>` entries below are load-bearing, not boilerplate. Two domains
   are held back from both cloud backup and device transfer:

   database   The Room database (shelfmates_database). This holds the bookmark
              wallet, redemption requests and reading progress. Backup rules are
              file-granular, so excluding the database also excludes reading
              progress: there is no way to keep the rows a user would want to
              carry to a new device while dropping the virtual-currency ledger.
              If cross-device reading progress becomes a requirement, the fix is
              to split the ledger/tables into a separate database file and keep
              this one excluded. See app/src/main/java/com/shelfmates/data/local.

   sharedpref Firebase Auth persists its session here. Backing it up would put
              bearer tokens in the user's cloud backup. The app itself stores no
              preferences of its own, so excluding the domain costs nothing.

   cacheDir is already excluded by Auto Backup by default, which covers the
   Supabase manuscript cache written by SupabaseStorageService.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="database" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="database" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
